{# How testing works: suites -> experiments -> results. `here` is the tab showing it. The
   <pre data-example> blocks are validated against the real schemas in the tests. #}
<details class="guide" id="howto">
  <summary>how testing works: suites → experiments → results</summary>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li class="{{ 'on' if here == 'suites' }}">
      <b>1 · write a suite</b> in <a href="/lab/suites">suites</a>: the requests and how each answer is scored.
      An item is a <code>prompt</code>, optionally the expected answer (<code>reference</code>), and an
      <code>evaluator</code>: the check that scores the answer from 0 to 1 and says pass or fail.
      Before measuring anything, <b>try it</b> on the chat model to see whether your checks score answers the way you expect.
    </li>
    <li class="{{ 'on' if here == 'test' }}">
      <b>2 · use it in an experiment</b> in <a href="/lab/test">test</a>: which models and llama.cpp settings answer the suite,
      and which phases run. <b>quality</b> scores answers, <b>latency</b> times them (synthetic suites),
      <b>bench</b> measures raw speed and needs no suite. The <b>matrix</b> varies settings (threads, KV cache…) to compare them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <b>3 · run it and compare</b> in <a href="/">results</a>: score and pass rate per configuration, next to speed,
      latency and memory. <b>gates</b> set pass/fail thresholds, and <b>guide</b> picks the winner and its llama-server command.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <div class="examples">
    <div>
      <p class="hint">the smallest suite: one question, one check</p>
      <pre data-example="suite">version: 1
name: capitals
endpoint: chat
source:
  items:
    - prompt: What is the capital of France? Answer with one word.
      reference: Paris
      evaluator: { type: exact, normalize: [strip, lower, strip_punct] }</pre>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="hint">an experiment that scores it with two quantizations</p>
      <pre data-example="experiment">version: 1
extends: [_profiles/pc.yaml]
experiment: { name: capitals-q4-vs-q8 }
models:
  - { id: q4, source: "hf://unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF:Q4_K_M" }
  - { id: q8, source: "hf://unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF:Q8_0" }
phases:
  bench: { enabled: false }
  quality: { enabled: true, suites: [../suites/capitals.yaml] }</pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
